  "body": "Part of #659. Filed on the maintainer's word (question dialog, 2026-11-12); ours either way: a theme (ours or anyone's) can only restyle what reads its tokens.\n\nAbout 51 places in `crates/ui` write a colour as a literal (`Color32::from_rgb(..)` and the like) instead of reading the theme (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs`); the list is in the estimate on #659 (comment of 2026-11-12). The verdict colours (gouge, rest, move kinds) and their colour-vision maths stay ours and stay as they are - they move into the token table, they do not change value.\n\nDone means: every such site reads a named token; a guard test fails on a new colour literal outside the token table (with an explicit, short allow-list if one is truly needed); every colour renders the same as before in dark and light and in each colour-vision mode (asserted on the token values; no snapshot PNG touched).",
